     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "A road cut across two parallel railway tracks.\n\"The road is a transversal,\" said the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "transversal",
     "corresponding",
     "alternate"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A line that cuts two or more lines is a transversal. When it cuts two parallel lines it makes pairs of equal angles: corresponding angles are equal and alternate interior angles are equal.\nCo-interior angles (on the same side inside) add up to 180 degrees.\nVertically opposite angles at a crossing are equal, and angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees."
    }
   },
